{"meta":{"engine":"This is LuaHBTeX, Version 1.21.0 (TeX Live 2025)","format":"lualatex"},"params":{"textwidth":23592960,"textheight":39046366,"topskip":[720896,0,0,0,0],"parskip":[0,65536,0,0,0],"parindent":1114112,"baselineskip":[891290,0,0,0,0],"oddsidemargin":3014656,"topmargin":1179648,"headheight":786432,"headsep":1638400,"footskip":1966080,"maxdepth":360448,"widowpenalty":150,"clubpenalty":150},"pages":[{"number":1,"pagewidth":40258437,"pageheight":52099153,"lines":[{"x":7750942,"y":11938692,"w":23592960,"h":798386,"d":233287,"text":" On Sorting Large Collections "},{"x":15868887,"y":13932624,"w":7357071,"h":642250,"d":275254,"text":" Priya Nandakumar "},{"x":7750942,"y":15541533,"w":23592960,"h":554435,"d":152568,"text":" September 9, 2022 "},{"x":7750942,"y":18190825,"w":23592960,"h":457441,"d":3932,"text":" Abstract "},{"x":9544989,"y":19436009,"w":20004866,"h":454820,"d":135004,"text":" We review the classical comparison-based sorting algorithms and"},{"x":9544989,"y":20222441,"w":20004866,"h":462029,"d":7209,"text":"discuss the information-theoretic lower bound that constrains all of"},{"x":9544989,"y":21008873,"w":20004866,"h":454820,"d":7209,"text":"them. "},{"x":7750942,"y":23271050,"w":23592960,"h":654940,"d":5662,"text":"1 Introduction "},{"x":7750942,"y":24873717,"w":23592960,"h":505921,"d":147830,"text":"Sorting is among the most thoroughly studied problems in computer science"},{"x":7750942,"y":25765007,"w":23592960,"h":538214,"d":179405,"text":"[Knu84]. Textbook treatments such as [1] describe dozens of methods, yet"},{"x":7750942,"y":26656297,"w":23592960,"h":505921,"d":147112,"text":"only a handful are used in practice. Detailed analysis of quicksort appears"},{"x":7750942,"y":27547587,"w":23592960,"h":538214,"d":179405,"text":"in [Knu84, p. 5], and a historical account of the subject can be found by"},{"x":7750942,"y":28438877,"w":23592960,"h":538214,"d":179405,"text":"consulting [Knu84, 1] together. "},{"x":7750942,"y":30701054,"w":23592960,"h":658715,"d":5662,"text":"2 A Lower Bound "},{"x":7750942,"y":32303721,"w":23592960,"h":513815,"d":147830,"text":"Any comparison sort must distinguish among n! possible orderings. Each"},{"x":7750942,"y":33195011,"w":23592960,"h":538214,"d":180598,"text":"comparison yields one bit, so at least log2(n!) comparisons are needed in the"},{"x":7750942,"y":34086301,"w":23592960,"h":505921,"d":147830,"text":"worst case. By Stirling’s approximation, "},{"x":13306670,"y":35698487,"w":12481505,"h":538214,"d":180598,"text":"log2(n!) = n log2 n \u0000 n log2 e + O(log n):"},{"x":30426784,"y":35698487,"w":917118,"h":538214,"d":179405,"text":"(1)"},{"x":7750942,"y":37310673,"w":23592960,"h":538214,"d":179404,"text":"Hence the number of comparisons is \n(n log n), as claimed in Section 3. "},{"x":7750942,"y":39572850,"w":23592960,"h":657771,"d":10381,"text":"3 Practical Considerations "},{"x":7750942,"y":41175517,"w":23592960,"h":498028,"d":147830,"text":"Real implementations care about caching and memory movement as much"},{"x":7750942,"y":42066807,"w":23592960,"h":513815,"d":139218,"text":"as about comparison counts. A simple verbatim sketch of insertion sort"},{"x":7750942,"y":42958097,"w":23592960,"h":505921,"d":7894,"text":"follows. "},{"x":7750942,"y":44439211,"w":23592960,"h":446359,"d":4306,"text":" for i = 1 to n-1: "},{"x":7750942,"y":45330501,"w":23592960,"h":498028,"d":163617,"text":" key = a[i] "},{"x":7750942,"y":46221791,"w":23592960,"h":446359,"d":163617,"text":" j = i - 1 "},{"x":7750942,"y":47113081,"w":23592960,"h":498028,"d":163617,"text":" while j >= 0 and a[j] > key: "},{"x":7750942,"y":49353212,"w":23592960,"h":477934,"d":0,"text":" 1 "}],"rules":[],"body":{"width":23592960,"height":39046366,"depth":0,"glueSign":1,"glueOrder":2,"glueSet":39150.1445,"items":[["o","whatsit"],["glue",720896,0,0,0,0,10],["h",0,0,0,0,""],["glue",1435238,0,0,0,0,0],["glue",-1435238,0,0,0,0,0],["p",-51],["glue",1435238,0,0,0,0,0],["glue",0,65536,0,0,0,3],["glue",0,0,0,0,0,3],["gl